window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>They lied. Played me in a way I wasn’t expecting at all.</p> <p>I made a mistake in trusting them, and that wouldn’t be happening again. If I could, I’d be far away from Ridgewood and the three men who crushed me in ways I didn’t think possible.</p> <p>But I’m not that lucky. Once again, I need them. This time I refuse to let them fill the cracks in my heart. They’re nothing but a step closer to my freedom. They want me here with them, but if they try to keep me, it’ll be a decision they regret.</p> <p>**Endgame is the second book in the Sapphire Duet. Book one, Runner, needs to be listened to first. This is an enemies to lovers dark romance with dark themes. This duet is interconnected to my Suncrest Bay series. Each can be listened to independently, but there are crossover characters. For more information about content of this Duet, please go to author's website.**</p>"; 
